- Create a list to store the values.
- If the current node is null, terminate the recursion.
- First, add the value of the current node.
- Then, visit the left subtree.
- After that, visit the right subtree.
- Return the list.
Time Complexity: O(n)

Each node is processed exactly once, so the time complexity depends on the total number of nodes.

Space Complexity: O(n) in the worst case, accounting for both the list and the recursion stack.

You could use a stack and an iterative DFS approach. However, the asymptotic time complexity will remain O(n).
